    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1432">

                <pb facs="1800" n="1600" xml:id="pg1600"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–3045</note>
                <head>No. 1432<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Text Submitted by the Soviet
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1432-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1432-f2"/>]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1945-08-01T23:59:59+03:00"
                            notBefore="1945-07-30T00:00:00+03:00">Undated</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft Entry for the
                    Protocol</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Declaration of the Soviet
                        Government Concerning the Soviet Prisoner-of-War Camp in the Cesenatico
                        District</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Italy</hi>)</p>
                <p>The Soviet delegation transmitted an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> on
                    this question to the delegations of the United States of America and Great
                        Britain<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1432-f3"/> (see enclosure No.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d1432-f4"/>).</p>
                <p>Prime Minister Churchill and Field Marshal Alexander gave a clarification on this
                        matter.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1432-f5"/> The Soviet delegation declared that
                    it considered this question closed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1432-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1432-f1-content">
                <p>Submitted to the Protocol Subcommittee. No section on this subject, however, was
                    included in the Protocol.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1432-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1432-f2-content">
                <p>Prepared for this volume by the Division of Language Services, Department of
                    State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1432-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1432-f3-content">
                <p>For the communication on this subject addressed to the United States Delegation,
                    see <ref target="#d1164">document No. 1164</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1432-f4" n="4" xml:id="d1432-f4-content">
                <p>Enclosure number blank in the original. The enclosure is identical to the
                    attachment to <ref target="#d1164">document No. 1164</ref>, except that it is
                    dated July 28, 1945.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1432-f5" n="5" xml:id="d1432-f5-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg367">pp. 367</ref>–<ref
                        target="#pg368">368</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
